    <VI_Package_Configuration_File>XCel Report Engine.vipc</VI_Package_Configuration_File>
    <Description>
      <One_Line_Description_Summary>Open XML-based Excel reporting engine for LabVIEW applications, with no dependencies on Microsoft Office, OLE, or ActiveX.</One_Line_Description_Summary>
      <Description>XCelReportEngine is a lightweight LabVIEW library for creating and modifying Microsoft Excel workbooks without requiring Microsoft Office, OLE, or ActiveX automation.
The package provides a LabVIEW API backed by a .NET Framework library that operates directly on Open XML documents. It supports creating reports from .xlsx workbooks and .xltx templates, selecting worksheets, reading and writing cells and ranges, inserting and formatting images, applying cell alignment, colors and borders, and protecting worksheet contents.
XCelReportEngine is designed as an alternative to the commonly used Excel functionality of the NI Report Generation Toolkit, while reducing deployment dependencies and failures caused by Office installation or update changes.
Formula evaluation, VBA execution, PDF conversion, and programmatic chart creation are not supported. Charts should be defined in the Excel template and populated through their source data ranges.</Description>
      <Copyright/>
      <Packager>Michele Santucci</Packager>
      <URL>https://github.com/weirdgyn/XCelReportEngine</URL>
      <Release_Notes/>
    </Description>
